<h1>Welcome to MAE Academy</h1>
<p>Model-Analyze-Engineering</p>
<p>Interactive labs for control systems, power electronics, and signal analysis — build intuition by running the model, not just reading about it.</p>
<p>Launch a Simulation</p>
<p>Explore Library</p>
<p>Engineering education becomes powerful when it remains close to the real system.</p>
<p>Engineering education becomes powerful when it remains close to the real system. MAE Academy turns abstract engineering curiosity into structured models, analytical clarity, and hands-on simulation.</p>
<p>Mohammad AbuElyan</p>
<p>Founder & Engineering Educator // MAE</p>
<p>Meet the founder and the MAE premise behind the platform: Model. Analyze. Engineering.</p>
<p>Meet the Founder & About MAE</p>
<p>Core Engineering Platforms</p>
<p>Three interconnected learning layers bridging rigorous mathematical theory with interactive, real-time hardware intuition.</p>
<p>Practical Simulations & Virtual Lab Benches</p>
<p>Bridge abstract mathematics with interactive, real-time physical simulation. Explore state transitions, transient settling curves, and feedback responses instantly in your browser.</p>
<p>Control Systems Simulator</p>
<p>Electrical Circuits Simulator</p>
<p>Power Electronics Simulator</p>
<p>Explore All Simulations</p>
<p>Open Textbooks & Engineering Manuals</p>
<p>Open textbooks, technical manuals, and foundational references in engineering, computing, mathematics, and physics, readable in the browser straight from open archives.</p>
<p>Electrical & Electronics</p>
<p>Computer Science</p>
<p>Robotics & Control</p>
<p>Mechanical & Structural</p>
<p>Explore Academic Library</p>
<p>Mathematical Research & System Identification</p>
<p>Open research notes, mathematical formulations, transfer functions, and algorithmic proofs behind our simulations. Grounded in numerical physics and validated against benchmark experiments.</p>
<p>Nonlinear System Identification</p>
<p>Dynamic Simulation Solvers</p>
<p>Algorithmic Derivations & Proofs</p>
<p>Explore Research Notes</p>
